{
  "id": "os-187",
  "title": "How to Fix the \"Bad System Config Info\" in Windows 10 - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The BAD_SYSTEM_CONFIG_INFO error is a </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-439\"><span>Blue Screen of Death</span></a><span> (BSOD) issue in </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-435\"><span>Windows </span></a><span>that appears with stop code 0x00000074. It usually occurs during startup and prevents the system from booting properly. This error indicates a problem with Windows system configuration, which may be related to corrupted files, drivers, or hardware components.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Common causes of the BAD_SYSTEM_CONFIG_INFO error include:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Loose or improperly connected internal cables</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Corrupted system files or damaged Windows registry entries</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Faulty, outdated, or incompatible </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-381\"><span>device drivers</span></a></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Corrupted Master Boot Record (MBR) or Boot Configuration Data (BCD)</span></li><li value=\"5\"><span>Incorrect system configuration settings</span></li><li value=\"6\"><span>Hardware failures such as defective RAM or hard drive issues</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"How-to-Fix-the-Bad-System-Config-Info-in-Windows-10\" height=\"621\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-1.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623141238/How-to-Fix-the-Bad-System-Config-Info-in-Windows-10.webp 1100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623141238/How-to-Fix-the-Bad-System-Config-Info-in-Windows-10-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623141238/How-to-Fix-the-Bad-System-Config-Info-in-Windows-10-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623141238/How-to-Fix-the-Bad-System-Config-Info-in-Windows-10-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623141238/How-to-Fix-the-Bad-System-Config-Info-in-Windows-10-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623141238/How-to-Fix-the-Bad-System-Config-Info-in-Windows-10-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623141238/How-to-Fix-the-Bad-System-Config-Info-in-Windows-10-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1100\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h2 id=\"how-to-fix-bad_system_config_info-on-windows\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>How to Trouble Shoot BAD_SYSTEM_CONFIG_INFO Error on Windows</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>To Come Out from Windows Error BAD_SYSTEM_CONFIG_INFO, the following guideline should be executed. We will start with the simple solution where we have to perform only System Restart.</span></p><h3 id=\"method-1-fix-windows-configuration-error-using-system-restart\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Method 1: Fix Windows Configuration Error Using System Restart</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Sometimes the issue is temporary.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Press and hold the Power button to shut down your PC.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Disconnect all external devices (USB, printer, external drives).</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Wait 1–2 minutes.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Reconnect devices and restart the system.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>If the issue persists, proceed to the next method</span></p><h3 id=\"method-2-fix-bad-system-config-info-by-resetting-windows-pc\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Method 2: Fix Bad System Config Info By Resetting Windows PC</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 1: </strong></b><span>Click on the Troubleshoot option to reset your PC.</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error-\" height=\"328\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-2.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144143/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error-.jpg 529w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144143/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error--100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144143/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error--200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144143/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error--300.jpg 300w\" width=\"529\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 2: </strong></b><span>Select Reset this PC.</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error_3\" height=\"289\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-3.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144455/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error_3.webp 526w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144455/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error_3-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144455/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error_3-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144455/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error_3-300.webp 300w\" width=\"526\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 3: </strong></b><span>Now, choose an option. We are selecting the Keep My Files option to remove apps and settings by keeping our personal files.</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error_2jpg\" height=\"363\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-4.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144314/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error_2jpg.webp 526w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144314/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error_2jpg-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144314/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error_2jpg-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623144314/Reset-PC-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error_2jpg-300.webp 300w\" width=\"526\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"method-3-uninstall-the-latest-updates-to-fix-system-windows-config-error\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Method 3: Uninstall the Latest Updates to Fix System Windows Config Error</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 1: </strong></b><span>Click on Troubleshoot option.</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Un\" height=\"328\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-5.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150644/Un.jpg 529w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150644/Un-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150644/Un-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150644/Un-300.jpg 300w\" width=\"529\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 2: </strong></b><span>Click the Advanced Options menu.</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Unistall-Latest-Updates-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error\" height=\"286\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-6.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150621/Unistall-Latest-Updates-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error.jpg 500w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150621/Unistall-Latest-Updates-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150621/Unistall-Latest-Updates-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150621/Unistall-Latest-Updates-to-Fix-Windows-Config-Error-300.jpg 300w\" width=\"500\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 3:</strong></b><span> Select Uninstall Updates option to remove recently installed updated from Windows</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"uninstall-latest-updates-to-fix-windows-config-error-(1)\" height=\"362\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-7.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623151317/uninstall-latest-updates-to-fix-windows-config-error-(1).webp 525w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623151317/uninstall-latest-updates-to-fix-windows-config-error-(1)-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623151317/uninstall-latest-updates-to-fix-windows-config-error-(1)-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623151317/uninstall-latest-updates-to-fix-windows-config-error-(1)-300.webp 300w\" width=\"525\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 4: </strong></b><span>Choose an Option as per your choice and proceed to uninstall recent updates.</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"uninstall-latest-updates-to-fix-windows-config-error_5\" height=\"337\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-8.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150915/uninstall-latest-updates-to-fix-windows-config-error_5.webp 525w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150915/uninstall-latest-updates-to-fix-windows-config-error_5-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150915/uninstall-latest-updates-to-fix-windows-config-error_5-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240623150915/uninstall-latest-updates-to-fix-windows-config-error_5-300.webp 300w\" width=\"525\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"method-4-fix-bad-system-config-info-by-memory-diagnostic\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Method 4: Fix Bad System Config Info by Memory Diagnostic</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> Search for the Windows Memory Diagnostic on the Windows Search bar. Now, open it.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"5--Open-Tool\" height=\"398\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-9.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093341/5--Open-Tool.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093341/5--Open-Tool-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093341/5--Open-Tool-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093341/5--Open-Tool-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> You will find the Restart Now &amp; Check For Problems option. Go for it to check for any issues on </span><a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/operating-systems/windows-memory-managment/#:~:text=The%20memory%20management%20in%20the,be%20allocated%20to%20each%20process.\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Windows Memory</span></a><span>.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"6--Click-Restart\" height=\"320\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-10.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093342/6--Click-Restart.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093342/6--Click-Restart-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093342/6--Click-Restart-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093342/6--Click-Restart-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><h3 id=\"method-5-run-sfc-command-to-fix-windows-configuration-error\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Method 5: Run SFC Command to Fix Windows Configuration Error</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> Search for the </span><a href=\"#/article/system-design/system-design-371\"><b><strong>Command Prompt</strong></b></a><span> &amp; open it.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"1--Command-Prompt\" height=\"325\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-11.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082858/1--Command-Prompt.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082858/1--Command-Prompt-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082858/1--Command-Prompt-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082858/1--Command-Prompt-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Execute the following command. It will check the entire data on the system whether any problem is there or not.</span></li></ul><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Command:</strong></b><span> sfc /scannow</span></p></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"3--SFC-Command\" height=\"114\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-12.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082859/3--SFC-Command.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082859/3--SFC-Command-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082859/3--SFC-Command-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082859/3--SFC-Command-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><h3 id=\"method-6-reset-driver-health-to-fix-bad-system-config-info\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Method 6: Reset Driver Health to Fix Bad System Config Info</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> In this case also, we need to open the </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-125\"><span>Command Prompt</span></a><span> on Windows.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"1--Command-Prompt\" height=\"325\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-13.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082858/1--Command-Prompt.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082858/1--Command-Prompt-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082858/1--Command-Prompt-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082858/1--Command-Prompt-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> The below-mentioned command should be used to check &amp; fix the Driver Heath if any problem is there.</span></li></ul><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Command:</strong></b><span> chkdsk C: /f</span></p></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"7--CHKDSK-Command\" height=\"146\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-14.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093343/7--CHKDSK-Command.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093343/7--CHKDSK-Command-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093343/7--CHKDSK-Command-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093343/7--CHKDSK-Command-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><h3 id=\"method-7-fix-windows-error-by-repairing-the-master-boot-record\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Method 7: Fix Windows Error by Repairing the Master Boot Record</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> On the Boot Menu after entering by pressing Del Key multiple times, click on the Troubleshoot option.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"1--Troubleshoot\" height=\"263\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-15.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093339/1--Troubleshoot.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093339/1--Troubleshoot-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093339/1--Troubleshoot-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093339/1--Troubleshoot-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Press the Advanced Options.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"2--Advanced-Options\" height=\"290\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-16.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/2--Advanced-Options.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/2--Advanced-Options-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/2--Advanced-Options-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/2--Advanced-Options-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 3:</strong></b><span> Select the </span><a href=\"#/article/system-design/system-design-375\"><span>Command Prompt</span></a><span> option.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"4--Command-Prompt\" height=\"232\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-17.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240403115547/4--Command-Prompt.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240403115547/4--Command-Prompt-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240403115547/4--Command-Prompt-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240403115547/4--Command-Prompt-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 4:</strong></b><span> Now, the following command will be used. It will fix the Master Boot Record of the system which might be also a potential reason behind the problem.</span></li></ul><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Command:</strong></b><span> bootrec /fixmbr</span></p></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"Bootrec-Command\" height=\"169\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-18.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240404112746/Bootrec-Command.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240404112746/Bootrec-Command-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240404112746/Bootrec-Command-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240404112746/Bootrec-Command-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><h3 id=\"method-8-fix-windows-config-error-using-advanced-options\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Method 8: Fix Windows Config Error Using  Advanced Options</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> On the Boot Menu, select the Troubleshoot option.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"1--Troubleshoot\" height=\"263\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-19.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093339/1--Troubleshoot.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093339/1--Troubleshoot-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093339/1--Troubleshoot-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093339/1--Troubleshoot-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Press the Advanced Options.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"2--Advanced-Options\" height=\"290\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-20.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/2--Advanced-Options.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/2--Advanced-Options-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/2--Advanced-Options-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/2--Advanced-Options-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 3:</strong></b><span> Click on the Startup Settings Option.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"3--Startup-Settings\" height=\"227\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-21.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/3--Startup-Settings.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/3--Startup-Settings-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/3--Startup-Settings-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405093340/3--Startup-Settings-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 4:</strong></b><span> After restarting, press Enter on the Last Known Good Configuration.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"1--Good-Configuration\" height=\"255\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-22.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240409110127/1--Good-Configuration.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240409110127/1--Good-Configuration-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240409110127/1--Good-Configuration-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240409110127/1--Good-Configuration-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><h3 id=\"method-9-fix-bad-system-config-info-on-windows-via-system-restore\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Method 9: Fix Bad System Config Info on Windows via System Restore</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> Search for the Recovery Under </span><a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/techtips/how-to-open-control-panel-on-windows-11/#:~:text=on%20OK%20button.-,Method%207%3A%20Open%20Control%20Panel%20in%20Windows%20Using%20Shortcut,the%20shortcut%20and%20click%20Finish.\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Control Panel</span></a><span> &amp; open it.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"5--Recovery\" height=\"281\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-23.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240408100131/5--Recovery.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240408100131/5--Recovery-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240408100131/5--Recovery-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240408100131/5--Recovery-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Click on the Open System Restore Option.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"12--Restore-Point\" height=\"147\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-24.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082903/12--Restore-Point.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082903/12--Restore-Point-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082903/12--Restore-Point-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082903/12--Restore-Point-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 3:</strong></b><span> Click on the Next to move ahead without any changes.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"13--Next\" height=\"316\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-25.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082904/13--Next.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082904/13--Next-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082904/13--Next-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082904/13--Next-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Step 4:</strong></b><span> Select Finish to start the Restoring Process of Windows.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"14--Finish\" height=\"317\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/os-187-img-26.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082904/14--Finish.png 400w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082904/14--Finish-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082904/14--Finish-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240405082904/14--Finish-300.png 300w\" width=\"400\"></p></div>",
  "textContent": "The BAD_SYSTEM_CONFIG_INFO error is a Blue Screen of Death (BSOD) issue in Windows that appears with stop code 0x00000074. It usually occurs during startup and prevents the system from booting properly. This error indicates a problem with Windows system configuration, which may be related to corrupted files, drivers, or hardware components.Common causes of the BAD_SYSTEM_CONFIG_INFO error include:Loose or improperly connected internal cablesCorrupted system files or damaged Windows registry entriesFaulty, outdated, or incompatible device driversCorrupted Master Boot Record (MBR) or Boot Configuration Data (BCD)Incorrect system configuration settingsHardware failures such as defective RAM or hard drive issues How to Trouble Shoot BAD_SYSTEM_CONFIG_INFO Error on WindowsTo Come Out from Windows Error BAD_SYSTEM_CONFIG_INFO, the following guideline should be executed. We will start with the simple solution where we have to perform only System Restart.Method 1: Fix Windows Configuration Error Using System RestartSometimes the issue is temporary.Press and hold the Power button to shut down your PC.Disconnect all external devices (USB, printer, external drives).Wait 1–2 minutes.Reconnect devices and restart the system.If the issue persists, proceed to the next methodMethod 2: Fix Bad System Config Info By Resetting Windows PCStep 1: Click on the Troubleshoot option to reset your PC. Step 2: Select Reset this PC. Step 3: Now, choose an option. We are selecting the Keep My Files option to remove apps and settings by keeping our personal files. Method 3: Uninstall the Latest Updates to Fix System Windows Config ErrorStep 1: Click on Troubleshoot option. Step 2: Click the Advanced Options menu. Step 3: Select Uninstall Updates option to remove recently installed updated from Windows Step 4: Choose an Option as per your choice and proceed to uninstall recent updates. Method 4: Fix Bad System Config Info by Memory DiagnosticStep 1: Search for the Windows Memory Diagnostic on the Windows Search bar. Now, open it.Step 2: You will find the Restart Now & Check For Problems option. Go for it to check for any issues on Windows Memory.Method 5: Run SFC Command to Fix Windows Configuration ErrorStep 1: Search for the Command Prompt & open it.Step 2: Execute the following command. It will check the entire data on the system whether any problem is there or not.Command: sfc /scannowMethod 6: Reset Driver Health to Fix Bad System Config InfoStep 1: In this case also, we need to open the Command Prompt on Windows.Step 2: The below-mentioned command should be used to check & fix the Driver Heath if any problem is there.Command: chkdsk C: /fMethod 7: Fix Windows Error by Repairing the Master Boot RecordStep 1: On the Boot Menu after entering by pressing Del Key multiple times, click on the Troubleshoot option.Step 2: Press the Advanced Options.Step 3: Select the Command Prompt option.Step 4: Now, the following command will be used. It will fix the Master Boot Record of the system which might be also a potential reason behind the problem.Command: bootrec /fixmbrMethod 8: Fix Windows Config Error Using  Advanced OptionsStep 1: On the Boot Menu, select the Troubleshoot option.Step 2: Press the Advanced Options.Step 3: Click on the Startup Settings Option.Step 4: After restarting, press Enter on the Last Known Good Configuration.Method 9: Fix Bad System Config Info on Windows via System RestoreStep 1: Search for the Recovery Under Control Panel & open it.Step 2: Click on the Open System Restore Option.Step 3: Click on the Next to move ahead without any changes.Step 4: Select Finish to start the Restoring Process of Windows.",
